    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T02:46:26Z",
    "body": "Fix (staged, uncommitted, awaiting main's review): new crates/motion/src/finishing3d/rim.rs adds a rim row. Between the outermost raster line with ground and its empty neighbour outward, the line offset is bisected (to tol/20) to where ground ends, and one extra line goes there when the gap is more than a quarter step. Grid lines don't move, and serpentine parity is kept (the rim row takes its empty neighbour's parity). Every sample goes through the same march, so the new row is as gouge-safe as any other line. Readings (release --ignored, finish3d + flow): tilted ramp 0.1698 -> 0. Every hill and dome fixture stays at 0. SCALLOP_RATCHET is now empty, so all fixtures answer to the 0.123 gate. Debug motion suite green, clippy -D warnings clean. golden_cl re-blessed for 2 goldens (finish3d_ramp_parallel_plateau +20 moves, finish3d_scallop_plateau +20 moves). Both are added rim rows only: on the flat plateau the old last row stood 1.31 mm inside the rim, which leaves a 0.30 mm rim sagitta for the raster on its own, and only the waterline ring had covered it.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
